;; Simon's mini game, Dracula's Castle: six screens of castle, then the throne room behind a
;; two-tile door. stage.ts loads it with ?raw, so it is not in the level library, the dev level
;; select or the campaign. Rows 0-1 stay empty under the Castlevania HUD; below them the air is
;; the crypt's black-brick backdrop (`H`, not solid, under an `A` cornice on row 2) with a few
;; open windows and stained glass. Dracula's room has Castlevania's tall barred windows and his
;; coffin on its stone dais.
;;
;; The route: the entrance hall (candles; one holds the dagger) -> stairs UP (18,12 rising right,
;; 5 tiles) onto the battlement walk (Medusa heads) -> stairs DOWN (50,12 rising left, 5 tiles)
;; into the bone hall (skeletons, a bat) -> the gallery (Medusa heads low) -> the
;; door (96, rows 11-12) -> Dracula. The wall at column 23 means the first flight must be climbed.
;; Candles, creatures and the Medusa heads' source are the mini game's own entity types (World's
;; extraEntities, stage.ts); `stairs` is World's. `door` and `dracula` are taken out of the map
;; and placed by the scene.
id: cv-castle
name: DRACULA'S CASTLE
world: 5
stage: 4
theme: crypt
music: cv-stage
time: 300
start: 2,12
startMode: stand
camera: scroll

